lector alone does not add links. Cancel discards all staged edits.","position":{"start":{"line":81,"column":1},"end":{"line":81,"column":1}},"key":"fRiaT8AYAg"}],"key":"zi3q8kGdjS"}],"key":"YpqEJI25rH"}],"label":"figure-multiple-edge-links","identifier":"figure-multiple-edge-links","enumerator":"3","html_id":"figure-multiple-edge-links","key":"NtPP4lXVNw"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":85,"column":1},"end":{"line":89,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The relation is ","position":{"start":{"line":85,"column":1},"end":{"line":85,"column":1}},"key":"RPvMzSNEOW"},{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":85,"column":1},"end":{"line":85,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"E_edge = selected peak μ + offset","position":{"start":{"line":85,"column":1},"end":{"line":85,"column":1}},"key":"m2U6TnwDiP"}],"key":"cIHdTa8ALt"},{"type":"text","value":". For peak μ = 285.00 eV,\nan offset of +0.20 gives E_edge = 285.20 eV; a negative offset places it below μ.\nIt is an exact offset, not an independent fitted separation. For EMG the source\nis its underlying μ, not its observed maximum. The model dE shifts both displayed\npositions consistently, without changing their native separation.","position":{"start":{"line":85,"column":1},"end":{"line":85,"column":1}},"key":"A9Ad8ldBy2"}],"key":"uHxnnzEHD8"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":91,"column":1},"end":{"line":98,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Linking replaces the edge’s independent position bounds/Free setting with the\nderived position; put absolute position bounds on the controlling peak’s μ.\nIn simultaneous fits, the edge’s global/per-spectrum scope follows that peak μ.\nTo change the peak or offset, reopen the same panel. An existing link’s peak and\noffset appear initially, even if another component is selected. To release the\nrelationship, select the edge, clear ","position":{"start":{"line":91,"column":1},"end":{"line":91,"column":1}},"key":"C9QZNSgcLY"},{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":91,"column":1},"end":{"line":91,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Link edge to peak μ","position":{"start":{"line":91,"column":1},"end":{"line":91,"column":1}},"key":"N4x7ViKcFj"}],"key":"HDjBZLZss0"},{"type":"text","value":" and Apply. This keeps the current derived edge\nenergy, makes E_edge free and resets its bounds to unbounded; review Min/Max/Free\nbefore fitting it independently. The link/unlink model edit can be undone.","position":{"start":{"line":91,"column":1},"end":{"line":91,"column":1}},"key":"fkuUrhhOz6"}],"key":"VHtsjycovb"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":100,"column":1},"end":{"line":111,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each edge can follow a different peak, or several edges can follow the same peak\nwith different signed offsets. Width, step and post-slope stay independently\nconfigured. All edges’ linked positions use the same native exact-offset convention\nand inherit the controlling peak’s effective global/per-spectrum scope in series fits.\nRenaming a controlling peak updates its edge links; unlink before removing a peak\nthat still controls an edge. Linked models retain these relationships when saved,\nreopened or exported. Linking a peak does not insert a missing physical feature into the data.\nIf the button is unavailable, check that at least one peak and edge exist.\nSelect the controlling peak inside the panel; no plot selection is required.\nAdd an edge rather than expecting the link command to create one. For\nlinks between peaks with a fitted separation interval, use the peak-constraint\nprocedure above instead.","position":{"start":{"line":100,"column":1},"end":{"line":100,"column":1}},"key":"oWGLBI9oWo"}],"key":"cyd8cHCAs3"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":113,"column":1},"end":{"line":113,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Links, sharing and saved models","position":{"start":{"line":113,"co